---
---

<section id="faq" class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <div class="text-center mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">
      Frequently Asked Questions
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Everything you need to know about our YAML formatter.</p>
  </div>
  <dl class="space-y-2">
    {[
      { q: 'What is a YAML formatter?', a: 'A YAML formatter takes messy, inconsistently-indented YAML and reformats it with consistent spacing, proper indentation, and clean structure without changing the data. It automatically fixes mixed tabs/spaces, aligns nested blocks, and normalizes whitespace.' },
      { q: 'Is my YAML data safe? Does it get uploaded?', a: 'No. Everything runs entirely in your browser using client-side JavaScript. Your YAML data is never transmitted to any server. You can verify this by disconnecting your internet after loading the page and the formatter will continue to work.' },
      { q: 'Can I convert YAML to JSON with this tool?', a: 'Yes. Click the "YAML to JSON" tab above the editor to instantly convert your YAML document to properly formatted JSON. The conversion handles nested objects, arrays, and complex data structures without data loss.' },
      { q: 'Does it support YAML anchors and aliases?', a: 'Yes. The parser fully supports YAML 1.2 anchors (&), aliases (*), and merge keys (<<). Both the anchor references and the resolved values are preserved in the formatted output.' },
      { q: 'Can I format multiple YAML documents at once?', a: 'Yes. YAML files can contain multiple documents separated by ---. Our formatter processes each document independently and preserves the document separators, which is especially useful for multi-resource Kubernetes manifests.' },
      { q: 'What YAML specification does this follow?', a: 'We follow the YAML 1.2 specification, which is the latest version. It resolves several ambiguities from YAML 1.1, including proper handling of booleans, null values, and octal number parsing.' },
      { q: 'Does this tool preserve YAML comments?', a: 'Yes. Comments in your YAML are preserved during formatting. They maintain their original position relative to the surrounding keys and values.' },
      { q: 'What keyboard shortcuts are available?', a: 'The editor supports standard keyboard shortcuts: Ctrl+Enter to format, Ctrl+Z/Ctrl+Y for undo/redo, Ctrl+F for search. Standard CodeMirror shortcuts for cut, copy, paste, and line operations are also supported.' },
      { q: 'Is this YAML formatter free?', a: 'Yes, completely free with no limits. No sign-up required, no usage caps, no premium tiers. The project is open source and will always remain free.' },
      { q: 'Can I use this tool offline?', a: 'Yes. Once the page is loaded, all processing happens locally in your browser. Disconnect from the internet and the formatter continues to work. For permanent offline access, clone the open-source repository.' },
      { q: 'Why does my YAML have indentation errors?', a: 'Common causes include mixing tabs and spaces (YAML only allows spaces), inconsistent indentation levels, or incorrect nesting of lists and mappings. Our editor highlights syntax errors in real-time with line-level precision.' },
      { q: 'How large a file can I format?', a: 'The tool handles files with thousands of lines efficiently. For extremely large files (10,000+ lines), formatting may take a moment. The CodeMirror editor is optimized for large documents and maintains smooth scrolling at any size.' },
    ].map(({q, a}) => (
      <div class="border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden transition-all duration-200">
        <dt>
          <button type="button" class="faq-toggle flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-4 text-left text-sm font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 hover:bg-zinc-50 dark:hover:bg-zinc-900/50 transition-colors" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>{q}</span>
            <svg class="faq-chevron w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
        </dt>
        <dd class="faq-answer hidden px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">{a}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-toggle').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const dd = btn.closest('div')?.querySelector('.faq-answer');
      const chevron = btn.querySelector('.faq-chevron');
      const isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!isOpen));
      if (dd) dd.classList.toggle('hidden');
      if (chevron) chevron.classList.toggle('rotate-180');
    });
  });
</script>
